{'symbol': 'GM', 'date': '2019-10-25 22:30:00', 'title': 'UNION APPROVES DEAL TO END GENERAL MOTORS 40-DAY STRIKE', 'text': "THE STRIKE AT US CAR MAKER GENERAL MOTORS HAS COME TO AN END AFTER THE WORKERS' UNION AGREED TO PASS A COLLECTIVE DEAL ON FRIDAY TO END THE LONGEST AUTOMOTIVE STRIKE IN 50 YEARS. AFTER STRIKING FOR 40 DAYS, THE UNITED AUTO WORKERS UNION (UAW) ANNOUNCED IN A STATEMENT LATE FRIDAY THAT THEY HAD VOTED IN FAVOUR OF PASSING A FOUR-YEAR LABOUR CONTRACT THAT WILL END THE WALKOUT. GM HAD ALREADY REACHED A PRELIMINARY AGREEMENT WITH THE UAW IN LAST WEEK, BUT THE EMPLOYEES STILL HAD TO RATIFY IT. THE RATIFIED CONTRACT INCLUDES A 11,000-DOLLAR SIGNING BONUS, TWO ANNUAL 3% WAGE INCREASES AND NO ADDITIONAL HEALTHCARE COSTS. THE STRIKE BEGUN ON SEPTEMBER 16, WITH MANY EMPLOYEES RESIGNING AFTER NEGOTIATIONS FAILED. THE WORKERS' DEMANDS HAD INCLUDED MORE AFFORDABLE HEALTH INSURANCE, JOB SECURITY AND FAIR PAY."}
